WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.860
Secure every camera with unique credentials, supported firmware, disabled unused services, and controlled administration.

2
00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:09.720
Avoid direct internet exposure.

3
00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:18.220
Segment camera, NVR, inference, storage, dashboard, and management networks according to required communication.

4
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:24.500
Remote access should use a managed entry point with strong authentication, authorization, and logs.

5
00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:34.120
Local servers need operating-system, driver, runtime, and model maintenance, least privilege, protected secrets, and a known-good rebuild process.

6
00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:40.240
Video and metadata may reveal people, routines, locations, and operations.

7
00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:51.620
Limit camera coverage to legitimate purposes, provide notice or consent where applicable, minimize retention, restrict live view and export, and audit access and configuration changes.

8
00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:59.980
Responsible use prohibits covert stalking, harassment, inappropriate surveillance, or attempts to identify private individuals without lawful authority.

9
00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:06.000
AI descriptions do not prove identity, intent, wrongdoing, or protected traits.

10
00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:08.100
Human reviewers remain accountable.

11
00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:22.460
Reliability monitoring should cover camera reachability, stream freshness, time synchronization, decode errors, inference queues, accelerator health, storage, event creation, dashboards, and alert delivery.

12
00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:28.560
Report degraded coverage clearly instead of presenting a healthy status while parts of the pipeline are blind.

13
00:01:28.840 --> 00:01:36.360
Plan failover, backup, and recovery for configuration, rules, model versions, and critical event records.

14
00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:39.740
Test component failure and capacity exhaustion.

15
00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:49.280
Secure operation means the system remains transparent about what it can see, protects what it stores, and recovers without weakening privacy or access controls.
